{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Nearest-Neighbor Texture Filtering.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Nearest-Neighbor Texture Filtering.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"nearest neighbor texture filtering nearest neighbor texture filtering","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Nearest-Neighbor Texture Filtering.md","fileName":"Nearest-Neighbor Texture Filtering.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Nearest-Neighbor Texture Filtering","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-20 23:34\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Advanced Real-Time Rendering]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Advanced Real-Time Rendering","gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Nearest-Neighbor Texture Filtering.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Nearest-Neighbor Texture Filtering.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"nearest neighbor texture filtering nearest neighbor texture filtering","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Nearest-Neighbor Texture Filtering.md","fileName":"Nearest-Neighbor Texture Filtering.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Nearest-Neighbor Texture Filtering","heading":"Nearest-Neighbor Texture Filtering","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Nearest-neighbor texture filtering chooses the texel center closest to a requested texture coordinate and returns that texel's value. It is inexpensive and preserves hard pixel boundaries.\n\nWhen a texture is magnified, the method produces visible blocks; when minified, it can flicker or alias because many source texels compete for one pixel. The look can be intentional for pixel art but unsuitable for smoothly detailed surfaces.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Advanced Real-Time Rendering","gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Nearest-Neighbo